{
  "id": "27776_nidasu",
  "headword": "{煮出|にだ}す",
  "reading": "にだす",
  "romaji": "nidasu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to brew; to boil to extract (flavor)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to brew; to boil to extract (flavor)",
      "explanation": "To boil an ingredient in water to draw out its flavor, color, or active components, as when making stock, tea, or herbal infusions."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27776_nidasu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{昆布|こんぶ}でだしを{煮出|にだ}す。",
      "english": "To boil kelp to make stock.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27776_nidasu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{麦茶|むぎちゃ}を{煮出|にだ}して{冷|ひ}やす。",
      "english": "I brew barley tea by boiling and then chill it.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27776_nidasu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{薬草|やくそう}をじっくり{煮出|にだ}すと、{独特|どくとく}の{香|かお}りが{広|ひろ}がる。",
      "english": "When you slowly boil the herbs, a distinctive aroma spreads.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Transitive godan verb. Xを{煮出|にだ}す. Compound of {煮|に}る (to boil) + {出|だ}す (to bring out). The {出|だ}す here means drawing the flavor out of the ingredient.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- だしを{煮出|にだ}す: to boil out stock\n- お{茶|ちゃ}を{煮出|にだ}す: to brew tea by boiling\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {煮込|にこ}む: to stew; to simmer — cooking the ingredient itself slowly, not extracting from it\n- {抽出|ちゅうしゅつ}する: to extract — a formal, technical term, not limited to boiling",
